  "result": "no_new_exact_named_child_role_or_physical_brake_binding; outer_component_metadata_scope_and_single_download_record_path_qualified",
  "newFindings": [
    {
      "claim": "The owner IVI outer ZIP has 38 members and the FSE outer ZIP has 11. The already-readable IVI Config manifest lists 35 package entries under Android, Mcu, Dsp, Anc and Screen; module declarations additionally include Camera. The plain FSE config is qc+mcu+dsp. These are IVI/FSE media-component package metadata, not a retained whole-car ECU package manifest.",
      "sourceKeys": [
        "archiveInventories",
        "componentManifest"
      ],
      "qualification": "A missing INS/FRL/domain-switch identity here proves only no exact binding in this finite outer metadata; encrypted/member payloads and arbitrary partitions were not searched."
    },
    {
      "claim": "None of the nine exact factory ECU IDs or complete nine-byte software codes appears in those outer inventories or sanitized readable-manifest attributes. No target component description can be joined from this source.",
      "sourceKeys": [
        "baseline",
        "componentManifest",
        "archiveInventories"
      ],
      "qualification": "No prefix/suffix inference, binary rescan or DID-number census was performed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "VersionUpdateStrategyHelper serializes an entire EcuVersionInfo through JSONUtil.toJson and SpUtil.putString. The actual caller uses the single key otaUpdateDownloadFileInfo in share_data_prefs; EcuVersionInfo includes ecuDescription, ecuId, ecuSoftCode, ecuUpgradePart, fileName and isSourcePackage. This is an additional source-backed candidate for a legitimately retained sanitized descriptive record.",
      "sourceKeys": [
        "versionDownloadCache",
        "sharePrefs",
        "configConsts",
        "ecuVersionModel",
        "checkVersionPresenter"
      ],
      "qualification": "No raw preference file or key value was acquired. Existence, content, completeness and present accessibility of this key remain unverified. The model also contains private material; only a fixed field-only projection could be useful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "That single download record may come from targetPackageInfo, configPackageInfo, sourcePackageInfo or configSourceInfo: all four feed mAllPackageInfo before index selection. It describes an update package and is not intrinsically an installed-unit or child-role identity.",
      "sourceKeys": [
        "checkVersionPresenter",
        "vehicleVersionModel"
      ],
      "qualification": "The download cache match compares ECU id, hashes, paths and filename; it does not by itself prove equality with an observed installed full software code or applicability to a child DID."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The retained approved export receipt records both GCY and GHY strategy.json as missing at its snapshot. It retained only four-byte and six-byte collect2 version-label files; source writes SourceVehicleVersion2 from strategy.strategyVer. They are not retained targetPackageInfo descriptions.",
      "sourceKeys": [
        "exportReceipt",
        "bootPresenter",
        "filePaths",
        "vehicleUtil"
      ],
      "qualification": "This is a historical receipt, not a current filesystem observation. ProductLineOTA strategy path has a separate prior investigation; it is not newly closed here. A new OTA/check/download must not be started merely to populate these caches."
    }
  ],
